WHAT IS COPIED
--------------
From upstream, in its own layout so `git diff` against block/buzz stays
meaningful: `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `Dockerfile`, `LICENSE`,
`migrations/`, `schema/`, and the relay with every workspace crate it depends
on: buzz-relay, buzz-audit, buzz-auth, buzz-conformance, buzz-core,
buzz-datastore-tracing, buzz-db, buzz-deletion, buzz-feature-flags,
buzz-media, buzz-pubsub, buzz-relay-mesh, buzz-sdk, buzz-search and
buzz-workflow. Also these single files:
- `previews/invite-video/` (two files), which the relay embeds;
- `.pgschemaignore`, `.env.example`, `test-fixtures/solo-creation.json`,
  `docs/nips/NIP-MP.fixtures.json`, `docs/sql/private-media-edit-preflight.sql`,
  `scripts/reconcile-schema-after-pgschema.sql`, `scripts/repair-events-pkey.sql`,
  `scripts/drop-partitioned-foreign-keys.sql`, `scripts/start-relay-for-tests.sh`,
  `scripts/seed-admin-dashboard.sh`,
  `scripts/maintenance/plan_duplicate_listed_channel_renames.sql` and
  `scripts/maintenance/rename_duplicate_listed_channel_names.sh`, which tests read;
- `scripts/maintenance/prebuild-media-edit-index.sql` and the operator documents
  migrations and startup refer to: `docs/database.md`,
  `docs/thread-window-deployment.md`, `docs/artifact-sync-deployment.md`,
  `docs/profile-search.md`, `docs/channel-name-uniqueness-deployment.md`,
  `docs/private-media-index-deployment.md` and
  `docs/trigger-retirement-deployment.md`.

Maxplayer's own: `crates/maxplayer-private-protocol/` (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
`NOTICE`, `README.md` and `.gitignore`.

Left behind (the relay does not build them): the AI-agent harness, push
gateway, device pairing, desktop / mobile / web clients, CLIs, and the other
upstream crates, scripts and docs.

MODIFICATIONS relative to block/buzz 298543f55
----------------------------------------------
Every copied upstream file not named below is byte-verbatim. Paths under
`crates/buzz-relay/src/` are shortened (`config.rs`, `api/git/transport.rs`).

Build and layout
- `Cargo.toml`: workspace `members` trimmed to the crates above plus
  `crates/maxplayer-private-protocol`; `exclude = ["desktop/src-tauri"]`
  dropped. No dependency or patch entry changed: upstream now pins every sqlx
  crate to one launchbadge/sqlx git revision, so the lock holds a single
  `sqlx-core` and nixpkgs' fetchCargoVendor can vendor it.
- `Cargo.lock`: upstream's lock, pruned to this workspace. Every version is
  upstream's; `maxplayer-private-protocol` is added.
- `crates/buzz-relay/Cargo.toml`: depends on `maxplayer-private-protocol`. The
  `buzz-cli` dev-dependency is dropped, and with it the one test module that
  drives the CLI, `api/media_access_postgres_tests/cli_edit_postgres_tests.rs`
  (removed; its `mod` line in `api/media_access_postgres_tests.rs` is a comment).
  The CLI and its crates are not vendored.
- `crates/buzz-db/src/runtime/migration.rs`: upstream tests that read paths not
  vendored skip them.

A. Open-relay fork (gudnuf/buzz)
- `BUZZ_OPEN_READ` (`config.rs`, `connection.rs`, `handlers/req.rs`,
  `api/bridge.rs`, `api/mod.rs`): an unauthenticated WebSocket connection may
  read stored history outside channels. It gets EOSE but no live subscription
  (it claims its ID like a one-shot search), an `#h`-scoped request gets an
  empty history, and the NIP-42 auth timeout does not close it. HTTP `/query`
  lifts only the relay-membership refusal; authentication, bans, NIP-FI
  refusals and channel checks still apply. Writes still need auth.
- `BUZZ_GIT_PUBLIC_READ` (off by default; `config.rs`, `api/bridge.rs`,
  `api/git/transport.rs`): git reads skip the relay-membership check, and HTTP
  `/query` serves repository events (kinds 30617/30618) to authenticated
  non-members from a channel-less fetch.
- `BUZZ_OPEN_INGEST` (off by default; `handlers/ingest.rs`): admit unknown
  event kinds with the messages-write scope.
- DVM job kinds 3400, 5109, 6109 and 7000 (`handlers/ingest.rs`).
- Git upload-pack fails closed (HTTP 500) on a non-zero exit or empty output,
  instead of a silent empty 200; its output is spooled to a file, not
  streamed (`api/git/transport.rs`).

B. Maxplayer
- Kinds (`handlers/ingest.rs`): the trade block 3401–3406, execution reviews
  3408/3409 and the seller heartbeat 30340 need messages-write; the NIP-89
  handler 31990 and the NIP-17 DM-relay list 10050 need users-write. Gift wraps
  (1059) and DM-relay lists are capped at 128 KB of content, and a gift wrap
  must carry a `p` tag (maxplayerai #397).
- Branch-scoped push tokens (maxplayerai #929): a NIP-98 git token may carry
  one `["ref", <refname>]` tag; the pre-receive policy then refuses any ref
  update that does not name exactly that ref (`api/git/transport.rs`,
  `api/git/hook.rs`, `api/git/policy.rs`). A scoped token with a NIP-40
  expiration lives up to `BUZZ_SCOPED_TOKEN_MAX_LIFETIME_SECS` (default 6 h);
  unscoped tokens keep upstream's ±120 s window (`crates/buzz-auth/src/nip98.rs`,
  `crates/buzz-auth/src/lib.rs`, `config.rs`). NIP-11 advertises the cap as
  `limitation.scoped_token_max_lifetime_secs` (`nip11.rs`).
- Private job and team repositories: the shared wire schemas
  (`crates/maxplayer-private-protocol/`), job ACLs
  (`crates/buzz-db/src/private_jobs.rs`, `crates/buzz-db/src/lib.rs`),
  provisioning and quotas (`api/git/private_jobs.rs`, `api/git/quota.rs`,
  `api/git/mod.rs`), and enforcement in `api/git/transport.rs` and
  `api/git/policy.rs`. A private repository never gets a relay-signed
  ref-state event (kind 30618; `api/git/transport.rs`), and a public
  announcement cannot use a private repository's id
  (`handlers/side_effects.rs`). Settings:
  `MAXPLAYER_PRIVATE_JOB_REPOS`, `MAXPLAYER_PRIVATE_SERVICE_PUBKEY`,
  `MAXPLAYER_TEAM_REPOS` (`config.rs`). See
  `docs/specs/private-offers-implementation.md` in maxplayerai.
- Incomplete history is never reported complete: a row that cannot be decoded
  fails the query (`crates/buzz-db/src/store/event.rs`). Upstream's REQ handler
  now ends a subscription whose history read failed with `CLOSED` itself.
- Tests: `api/git/private_jobs_http_tests.rs`,
  `api/git/private_quota_cas_tests.rs`, `handlers/req_maxplayer_tests.rs`,
  `crates/buzz-db/src/store/history_failure_tests.rs`, and a test helper in
  `state.rs`.

C. Migrations
- Maxplayer migrations use versions from 100000 up, after every upstream one.
  `100025_private_job_repositories.sql` is the pre-merge fork's 0025 byte for
  byte; before migrating, `crates/buzz-db/src/runtime/migration.rs` moves a
  database's version-25 record to 100025 when its stored checksum is that
  migration's (any other version-25 record is left for sqlx to reject).
  `100027` adds the session column.
- Upstream's 0090 retires the community write fence: it drops the fence
  triggers it knows by name, then the fence functions without CASCADE. The
  private-job table carries one more fence trigger, so `migration.rs` drops it
  right before 0090 runs. `100026_private_job_repositories_write_fence.sql`,
  which attached that trigger, is now a no-op (on a fresh database 0090 runs
  first and the function is gone); a database that applied the original keeps
  its record, and `migration.rs` moves its stored checksum to the new file's
  only when it is the original's. `100028` drops the table's one foreign key,
  as upstream's 0101–0104 do for theirs (docs/database.md Rule 2). The
  schema-object lint exempts 100025–100027, which production applied before
  the rule.
- The table is in the deletion catalog (`crates/buzz-db/src/store/deletion.rs`)
  and the desired-state schema (`schema/schema.sql`,
  `schema/tables/public/private_job_repositories.sql`).
- Upstream's git read gate (SEC-005) denies a repository not bound to a
  channel. Maxplayer binds none, so those stay readable to every caller the git
  auth admits; channel-bound repositories keep upstream's membership gate, and
  private job repositories keep their job ACL (`api/git/transport.rs`).
